payload.text:
### MANDATORY CHANGE REPORT

1️⃣ **Exact file(s) modified**
*   `store.tsx`
*   `pages/CommandesGros.tsx`

2️⃣ **Exact line(s) changed**
*   **`store.tsx`**: 
    *   Line 110: Updated `updateGros` definition in `AppState` interface.
    *   Lines 231-248: Refactored `updateGros` implementation to fix the race condition and correctly handle object-based updates.
*   **`pages/CommandesGros.tsx`**: 
    *   Lines 255, 258, 261, 266, 268, 271, 276, 283: Updated all calls to `updateGros` to pass an object instead of two separate arguments.

3️⃣ **Before vs After code snippet**

**`store.tsx` (Update Logic)**
*   *Before*:
    ```tsx
    const updateGros = useCallback(async (id: string, field: keyof CommandeGros, value: any) => {
      let item: CommandeGros | undefined;
      setGros(p => p.map(i => {
        if (String(i.id) === String(id)) { item = { ...i, [field]: value }; return item; }
        return i;
      }));
      if (supabase && item) await supabase.from('commandes_gros').update(computeGrosCalculatedFields(item)).eq('id', id);
    }, []);
    ```
*   *After*:
    ```tsx
    const updateGros = useCallback(async (id: string, updates: Partial<CommandeGros>) => {
      setGros(prev => {
        const currentItem = prev.find(i => String(i.id) === String(id));
        if (!currentItem) return prev;
        const updatedItem = { ...currentItem, ...updates };
        if (supabase) {
          supabase.from('commandes_gros')
            .update(computeGrosCalculatedFields(updatedItem))
            .eq('id', id)
            .then(({ error }) => { if (error) console.error("Supabase update error:", error); });
        }
        return prev.map(i => String(i.id) === String(id) ? updatedItem : i);
      });
    }, []);
    ```

**`pages/CommandesGros.tsx` (Checkbox Call)**
*   *Before*:
    ```tsx
    onClick={() => updateGros(item.id, 'processed', !item.processed)}
    ```
*   *After*:
    ```tsx
    onClick={() => updateGros(item.id, { processed: !item.processed })}
    ```

4️⃣ **Why the bug occurred**
The `item` variable used for the Supabase update was being assigned inside the asynchronous state setter closure (`setGros(p => ...)`). In React, state updates are batched and processed asynchronously. The code following the `setGros` call executed immediately, while `item` was still `undefined`. Consequently, the `if (supabase && item)` check failed every time, and no data was ever sent to Supabase.

5️⃣ **Confirmation**
*   **Financial logic unchanged**: Confirmed.
*   **Realtime sync unchanged**: Confirmed (The existing subscription automatically catches the DB change).
*   **No schema changes made**: Confirmed.
*   **Field is operational-only**: Confirmed.

**Does this change affect Encaisse, Attendu, Pertes, or any KPI?**
No.

